    "explanation": "Q1 calculates the minimum absolute difference between any two distinct X values, while Q2 calculates the minimum positive difference where A.X > B.X. The key difference is that Q1 considers both positive and negative differences (taking absolute value), whereas Q2 only considers positive differences where A.X > B.X. Additionally, Q1 excludes pairs where X values are equal, while Q2 excludes pairs where A.X ≤ B.X.",
