explanation:
{
    "explanation": "Q1 uses correlated subqueries to check adjacent seats individually, returning seat IDs where the seat itself is free AND at least one adjacent seat (either seat_id-1 OR seat_id+1) is free. Q2 uses a self-join with conditions that match pairs of adjacent free seats, returning both seat IDs from each pair. The key difference is that Q1 returns seat IDs where the seat is free and has at least one free neighbor, while Q2 returns all seat IDs that are part of any adjacent free pair (which includes both seats in each pair).",
